description:
Give repository actions one constructor that returns a file write only when the captured entry does not already hold the bytes and mode, and use it wherever a materializer makes that comparison.

## Background

- The comparison "captured entry is a file with these bytes and this mode, so emit nothing; otherwise `WriteFile` with `ExpectedPreimage::of(entry)`" is written at:
  - configured projections (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/materialize.rs:365-378`);
  - the data-root ignore file (`materialize.rs:444-458`);
  - default schemas (`materialize.rs:541-553`), plus a string comparison of `rules.toml` against its current text (`:520-528`);
  - profile repair (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/mod.rs:1047-1061`);
  - the gate-registry edit in the mutation finalizer (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/mutation.rs:983-999`);
  - package-tree capture, deciding `TreeFileDisposition` (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/package_tree.rs:271-296`);
  - `composed_target_disposition` deciding `ProfileTargetDisposition` (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/profile_apply.rs:1926-1941`).
- The only plain constructor, `RepositoryAction::write_file` (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/image.rs:1137-1151`), is test-only. Action owners are the `RepositoryActionOwner` enum.

## Success Criteria

- [hard] REQ-01: `RepositoryEntry` has one predicate saying whether it is a file holding given bytes and mode, and `RepositoryAction` has one production constructor returning `Some(WriteFile)` with the entry's preimage when the predicate fails and `None` when it holds.
- [hard] REQ-02: The projection, ignore-file, rules, schema, profile-repair and gate-registry sites build their writes through that constructor, and the package-tree and profile dispositions derive "unchanged" from the predicate; no other code compares a captured file's bytes and mode to decide a write.
- [hard] REQ-03: Unit tests of the constructor cover an absent entry, an equal file, a file differing in bytes, a file differing in mode, and a directory occupant.

## Notes

- Behaviour is unchanged: each site emits the same actions for the same image.
- Written against the code as it stands after the changes this one follows; line citations name current code.
